  <div class="eyebrow eyebrow-red">Policies</div>
  <h1>Environmental policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">A roof should last decades, and the way it is built should do as little harm as possible. This statement sets out how {{ site.name }} manages the environmental side of its work, and what we are doing to improve.</p>
  <p class="updated">Last updated 10 November 2026 · reviewed every year</p>

  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>{{ site.name }} is a trading name of {{ site.ownerFullName }}, a sole trader roofer working across {{ site.areasLong }}. We will:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Meet or go beyond every environmental law and regulation that applies to our work.</li>
    <li>Reduce waste, and recycle or reuse what we can.</li>
    <li>Keep travel, fuel use and emissions down.</li>
    <li>Choose durable, responsibly sourced materials.</li>
    <li>Prevent pollution on site and protect wildlife.</li>
    <li>Review this policy every year and keep improving.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Repair before replace</h2>
  <p>The greenest roof is often the one already there. Where a repair will give a sound, lasting result, we will say so rather than recommend a full re-roof. Good slates, tiles and ridges are salvaged and reused wherever they are fit for it.</p>

  <h2>Waste</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Old slate, tile, timber, metal and felt are separated on site so they can be recycled or reused.</li>
    <li>Waste we can't reuse goes to licensed waste carriers and sites only, and we keep waste transfer notes as the law requires.</li>
    <li>We order materials to measure to avoid offcuts and surplus, and return unused materials to suppliers where we can.</li>
    <li>Hazardous materials, including any suspected asbestos, are never disturbed by us. We stop work and arrange a licensed specialist.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Materials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We favour natural slate and long-life materials that cut how often a roof needs replacing.</li>
    <li>We buy from local merchants where we can, which cuts delivery miles and supports the local economy.</li>
    <li>Where timber is used, we choose timber from certified sustainable sources (FSC or PEFC).</li>
    <li>On flat roofs we fit long-life systems (EPDM rubber and GRP fibreglass) and follow the makers' instructions for adhesives and resins, so nothing harmful runs off.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Travel and energy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We plan jobs and material runs together to keep mileage down, and work locally across west Wales.</li>
    <li>Vehicles are kept serviced and tyres kept at the right pressure, and we don't leave engines idling.</li>
    <li>When the van is replaced, we will look at lower-emission options.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>On site</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Sites are left clean and swept, with no debris left in gutters, gardens or drains.</li>
    <li>Fuels, resins and adhesives are stored and handled so they can't spill into drains or watercourses.</li>
    <li>Bats, nesting birds and their roosts are protected by law. If we find signs of them we stop, and we follow the advice of Natural Resources Wales.</li>
    <li>We keep noise and disruption to neighbours to a minimum.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Net zero</h2>
  <p>We support the UK and Welsh targets of net zero greenhouse gas emissions by 2050. As a small business our biggest sources are fuel and materials. The measures above are how we reduce both, and we will add to them as lower-carbon options become practical.</p>

  <h2>Responsibility</h2>
  <p>{{ site.ownerFullName }} is responsible for this policy and for making sure anyone working with us follows it. Questions are welcome: <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
